/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (Kruskal's Algorithm was successfully implemented to find the Minimum Spanning Tree of a weighted graph. The algorithm uses a greedy approach by selecting edges in increasing order of weight while avoiding cycles. The use of the Disjoint Set \(Union-Find\) data structure makes cycle detection efficient. The algorithm has a time complexity of O\(E log E\) due to sorting the edges. )
